 34MG    1H(34MG,34MG'G):BETA2:XUNDL-5 2014MI09                           201405
 34MG c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2014Mi09:                          
 34MG2c  Phys Rev C 89, 054307 (2014)                                           
 34MG c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), May 7, 2014                           
 34MG c  Beam={+34}Mg at 51.1 MeV/nucleon, target=liquid hydrogen. Proton-proton
 34MG2c  inelastic scattering in inverse kinematics used to determine           
 34MG3c  deformation length and |b{-2} for first 2+ state                       
 34MG c  {+34}Mg produced by fragmentation of 63 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam       
 34MG2c  with {+181}Ta and enriched {+64}Ni target foils of 150 |mm and         
 34MG3c  200 |mm thicknesses, respectively at RFQ-RILAC-CSM-RRC accelerator     
 34MG4c  at RIKEN facility. The fragments were separated and identified by RIPS 
 34MG5c  fragment separator optimized for A/Z=3 reaction products. Particle     
 34MG6c  identification was made from measurements of magnetic rigidity (B|r),  
 34MG7c  time-of-flight (tof), and energy loss (|DE-E). The secondary beam      
 34MG8c  of {+34}Mg at 51.1 MeV/nucleon hit a liquid hydrogen target (CRYPTA).  
 34MG9c  The scattered particles were analyzed by the TOMBEE spectrometer       
 34MGAc  consisting of a superconducting triplet quadrupole, plastic            
 34MGBc  scintillator, and a |DE-E telescope of a silicon detector and a NaI(Tl)
 34MGCc  detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin using DALI2 array of 160 NaI(Tl)
 34MGDc  detectors surrounding the hydrogen target. In order to apply Doppler   
 34MGEc  correction to the measured |g-ray energies, angles of the |g rays were 
 34MGFc  measured relative to the trajectories of the scattered particles. The  
 34MGGc  scattering angles were measured using two parallel-plate avalanche     
 34MGHc  counters (PPAC) upstream and one PPAC detector downstream from the     
 34MGIc  {+1}H target. Deduced deformation lengths and |b{-2} deformation       
 34MGJc  parameter from the analysis of measured angle-integrated cross section 
 34MGKc  by coupled-channel calculations with the ECIS97 computer code, and WP09
 34MGLc  global potential. Comparison with shell-model (SDPF-M) calculations,   
 34MGMc  and with previous experimental results                                 
